WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.207
Let’s create a list of five scores.

00:00:02.207 --> 00:00:06.692
The square brackets tell Python that these values belong to one list.

00:00:06.692 --> 00:00:09.552
Printing the list shows the full collection.

00:00:09.552 --> 00:00:12.362
Len tells us there are five values.

00:00:12.362 --> 00:00:16.720
Max returns ninety-one, and min returns sixty-nine.

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:24.627
A list is a good choice here because scores may be added, removed, sorted, or updated later.

00:00:24.627 --> 00:00:28.987
Try adding another score and rerun the summary functions.

00:00:28.987 --> 00:00:32.589
Notice that the same code adapts to the larger collection.
